@page "/changelog"
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.AllowAnonymous]
@layout GoatLab.Client.Layout.LandingLayout

<PageTitle>Changelog — GoatLab</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="What's new in GoatLab — feature releases, improvements, and bug fixes." />
</HeadContent>

@* ---------- HERO ---------- *@
<section class="cl-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.NewReleases" Style="font-size:16px;" />
            <span>Changelog</span>
        </div>
        <h1>What we've shipped recently.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            New entries on top. Anything tagged <strong>Feature</strong> is something you can do
            today that you couldn't yesterday. <strong>Improvement</strong> means existing flows
            got faster, smarter, or less broken.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

@* ---------- ENTRIES ---------- *@
<section class="cl-entries">
    <div class="container">

        @* When you ship something user-visible, prepend a new <article class="cl-card"> here.
           Keep entries concise — one sentence per bullet, link to docs/blog from the site if needed. *@

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-05-08</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-improvement">Improvement</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Brand refresh + reliability polish</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>New brand mark.</strong> Watercolor goat replaces the abstract icon in the navbar, footer, splash, and PWA install icons. The same goat appears as a heritage seal lockup on marketing surfaces and the social card.</li>
                <li><strong>Self-host is two curls.</strong> Self-hosters no longer clone the whole repo — grab <code>docker-compose.oss.yml</code> and <code>.env.example</code> directly from the repo and you're running. The Docker Hub image gets multi-arch builds (amd64 + arm64) on every release tag.</li>
                <li><strong>Admin console doesn't hang silently anymore.</strong> Every admin page surfaces a real error message if an API call blips, instead of an indefinite spinner. Tenant + user search filters as you type.</li>
                <li><strong>Smaller polish.</strong> Pricing section shows a graceful fallback when the billing API is briefly unavailable. Footer brand mark links to home. Dashboard activity feed got a more detailed goat silhouette. Audit-log target links no longer dead-end on entries that don't have a detail page.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-05-07</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>GoatLab is now open source — self-host on your own hardware</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>MIT-licensed source on <a href="https://github.com/chrisdfennell/GoatLabSaaS" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</strong> Pull the prebuilt image from <a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/fennch/goatlab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docker Hub</a> (multi-arch, runs on a Raspberry Pi or arm64 NAS) or clone the repo and build from source — both paths run the same app you see here.</li>
                <li>Self-host mode unlocks every feature for every tenant on the instance. No Stripe, no plan tiers, no marketplace; your data lives in your own Docker volumes.</li>
                <li>No lock-in. If you ever want to migrate off goatlab.app, export your farm to CSV, spin up the container, and import — same data, same UI.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-30</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Searchable marketplace, vet share-links, cross-farm lineage</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Filterable breed pages:</strong> <a href="/breeds">/breeds/{breed}</a> now shows individual goats with filters (sex, price, state, sort). Each listing card links straight to the goat detail.</li>
                <li><strong>Follow this farm:</strong> buyers can drop their email on any public farm page and get one notification when that farm lists a new goat. No daily digests, no marketing — operational only. Unsubscribe in one click from any email.</li>
                <li><strong>Vet share-links:</strong> from a goat's detail page, click "Share with vet" to mint a time-bounded URL the vet can open without signing up. They see medical, weight, FAMACHA, and body-condition history, plus a form to leave a note that lands on your timeline. Optional: GoatLab can email the link directly to the vet.</li>
                <li><strong>Cross-farm lineage:</strong> every for-sale or transferred goat has a public <a href="/breeds">/lineage/{id}</a> page that walks pedigree four generations deep. Ancestors with registration numbers link to whichever public GoatLab farm currently holds that animal — click any underlined name to walk the line. The closest thing to a "Carfax for goats."</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-27</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Goat timeline view, faster public listings, search-friendly farm pages</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Every goat has a new <strong>Timeline</strong> tab that combines medical records, weights, FAMACHA scores, milk production, breeding events, kiddings, shows, photos, and status changes into one chronological scroll — grouped by month and color-coded by severity.</li>
                <li>Public farm pages and individual for-sale listings (<code>/pub/{your-farm}</code> and <code>/pub/{your-farm}/{goat}</code>) now render server-side, so Google, Facebook, and link-preview unfurlers see real content (photos, prices, breed, pedigree) instead of a loading spinner. Faster first paint for buyers too.</li>
                <li>Each public goat listing now ships <code>schema.org Product</code> structured data with price, availability, and breed — making your for-sale animals eligible for rich Google search results.</li>
                <li>Reserve-with-deposit on public listings now works without JavaScript — buyers fill a form, hit submit, and go straight to Stripe Checkout.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-26</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-improvement">Improvement</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Accurate mortality timestamps + admin backup visibility</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Mortality reports now use the goat's actual status-change moment instead of approximating from <code>UpdatedAt</code>.</li>
                <li>Admins can see the offsite-backup last-success state and trigger a manual run from <code>/admin/health</code>.</li>
                <li>Terms and Privacy entity name, contact, and jurisdiction are now configurable without a code redeploy.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-25</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Farm-to-farm transfers, mate recommendations, breed directory</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Send a goat (and its medical/weight/milk/photo history) to another GoatLab farm via a secure token link.</li>
                <li>For each doe, GoatLab now ranks every intact buck in your herd by projected offspring COI plus daughter production.</li>
                <li>New public breed directory at <a href="/breeds">goatlab.app/breeds</a> aggregating for-sale listings across every farm with a public profile.</li>
                <li>Server-prerendered breed pages so the directory shows up properly in search engines.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-22</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Online reservations, QR ear-tag sheets, withdrawal tracking</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Public listings can take a Stripe-Checkout deposit to reserve an animal — buyer goes straight onto the seller's waitlist with the deposit recorded.</li>
                <li>Print a sheet of QR codes for every goat in your filtered list — each scans to that goat's profile.</li>
                <li>Medication withdrawal periods now block sales and milk logging until the hold expires, with a tenant-wide "active holds" view on the health dashboard.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-19</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Buyer waitlist, deposits, and a buyer portal</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Track interested buyers with breed/sex preferences, deposit amounts, and priority. Convert to a sale in one click.</li>
                <li>Buyers can view their place on your waitlist via a magic-link portal — no account required.</li>
                <li>Inline customer creation from the waitlist dialog so you can add a new buyer without leaving the form.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-18</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>API keys, outbound webhooks, feed consumption</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Generate tenant API keys (one-shot reveal) and authenticate against the same endpoints your browser uses.</li>
                <li>Subscribe to webhooks for goat / sale / kidding / medical events with HMAC-SHA256 signatures and 3-attempt retries.</li>
                <li>Track feed consumption against inventory; the reorder forecast warns you before you run out.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="cl-card">
            <div class="cl-card-meta">
                <span class="cl-date">2026-04-17</span>
                <span class="cl-tag cl-tag-feature">Feature</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Reports, forecasting, and progeny rollups</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Six new reports on the Insights tab: P&amp;L, milk trends, kidding, mortality, parasite/FAMACHA, health spend.</li>
                <li>Forecasts for kidding load, milk production, and 90-day cash flow based on trailing averages.</li>
                <li>Per-sire / per-dam offspring rollups so you can see which animals are actually producing.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <div class="cl-footer-card">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Lightbulb" Style="font-size:24px;color:#2e7d32;" />
            <div>
                <strong>Need something that's not here?</strong>
                <a href="mailto:@LegalSettingsService.Or(_settings?.ContactEmail, "CONTACT EMAIL")">Email us</a>
                and we'll add it to the roadmap.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .cl-hero {
        background:
            radial-gradient(1100px 360px at 50% 0%, rgba(102,187,106,0.15), transparent),
            #fff;
        padding: 80px 0 32px;
        text-align: center;
    }
    .cl-hero .container { max-width: 880px; padding: 0 28px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .cl-hero .eyebrow {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
        background: rgba(46,125,50,0.10); color: #2e7d32;
        padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 999px;
        font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.3px;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .cl-hero h1 {
        font-size: 48px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -1.5px;
        color: #102a1a; margin: 0 0 14px;
    }
    .cl-hero .lede {
        font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3a4a3e;
        max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;
    }
    @@media (max-width: 720px) {
        .cl-hero { padding: 56px 0 24px; }
        .cl-hero h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    }

    .cl-entries { padding: 24px 0 80px; background: #fff; }
    .cl-entries .container { max-width: 880px; padding: 0 28px; margin: 0 auto; }

    .cl-card {
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 26px 28px;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
        transition: border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
    }
    .cl-card:hover {
        border-color: rgba(46,125,50,0.35);
        box-shadow: 0 10px 28px -16px rgba(16,42,26,0.18);
    }
    .cl-card-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .cl-card h2 {
        font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.4px;
        color: #102a1a; margin: 4px 0 12px;
    }
    .cl-card ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
    .cl-card li { margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: #2a3a2e; }
    .cl-card a { color: #2e7d32; }
    .cl-card code {
        background: rgba(46,125,50,0.10); color: #1b5e20;
        padding: 1.5px 6px; border-radius: 5px;
        font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9em;
    }

    .cl-date { font-size: 13px; color: #6b7a70; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 500; }
    .cl-tag {
        font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase;
        padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 700;
    }
    .cl-tag-feature     { background: #e6f4ea; color: #1b5e20; }
    .cl-tag-improvement { background: #e3f2fd; color: #0d47a1; }
    .cl-tag-fix         { background: #fff3e0; color: #b25400; }

    .cl-footer-card {
        display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 14px;
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(46,125,50,0.06), rgba(102,187,106,0.10));
        border: 1px solid rgba(46,125,50,0.20);
        border-radius: 14px;
        padding: 18px 22px;
        margin-top: 24px;
        font-size: 15px; color: #2a3a2e; line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .cl-footer-card strong { color: #102a1a; display: block; margin-bottom: 2px; }
    .cl-footer-card a { color: #2e7d32; }

    @@media (max-width: 720px) {
        .cl-card { padding: 22px; border-radius: 14px; }
        .cl-card h2 { font-size: 19px; }
    }
</style>

@code {
    private GoatLab.Shared.DTOs.LegalSettingsDto? _settings;

    [Inject] private LegalSettingsService Legal { get; set; } = default!;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _settings = await Legal.GetAsync();
    }
}
